        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c575b05c-d48e-5d99-8135-064d57393faa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jeremiah Meyer, Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz, King George III\n- Organizations: Royal Academy\n- Roles: Painter in Miniatures, Painter in Enamels, Queen of Great Britain and Ireland, Queen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland\n- Places: Great Britain, Ireland, United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland\n\nFacts:\n- Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz was born on 19 May 1744 and died on 17 November 1818.\n- Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz became Queen of Great Britain and Ireland by marrying King George III in 1761.\n- Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz was Queen of Great Britain and Ireland from 1761 until the union of Great Britain and Ireland in 1801.\n- From 1801 until her death in 1818, Charlotte of Mecklenburg-Strelitz was Queen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.\n- Jeremiah Meyer served as Painter in Miniatures to Queen Charlotte.\n- Jeremiah Meyer served as Painter in Enamels to King George III.\n- Jeremiah Meyer was one of the founder members of the Royal Academy.",
